            "review_text": "Mike B\nNew York4 contributions\n0\nGreat Sandwiches, Fun Experience\nDec 2019 • Solo\nI happened to walk by this shop on my last day in Hanoi. To make it more fun there was a SEA games soccer match on between Vietnam and Cambodia. I was fortunate enough to be seated next to a group of Vietnamese people there for the game. The outcome was I got to eat a great sandwich on excellent bead and have a meaningful experience with locals while the game was on. I basically ended up there for 3 hours, rooted for Vietnam, and drank with locals. There was a language barrier but watching sports and exchanging simple conversation in this place was great. 4 beers and a sandwich cost me $5 USD...The place is in a nice location just outside where the large crowds are for the night market.\nRead more\nWritten December 13, 2019",
