            "review_title": "Review at Smile Bread Coffee",
            "review_text": "L Charles\n27 contributions\n0\nGood food but lying chef!\nNov 2019 • Couples\nStumbled upon this place, greeted by friendly man with banh mi menu all looked great. \n\nOrdered 1 egg Banh mi and 1 ‘footlong’ chicken Banh mi. \n\nWaited a fair bit of time, then were presented with 2 identical sized breads. We told the chef we had ordered one to be footlong (more expensive) and the waiter had previously confirmed with us. \n\nInstead of an apology, we were met with a defensive bunch of rubbish about how in Vietnam foot long actually means the same size and their foot long baguette is a meat special with three different types of meat however she had only prepared it with chicken and what became immediately obvious is that they had run out of the larger bread sizes.\n\nInstead of apologising and admitting that they had run out of the correct bread the chef continued to lie to us trying to explain why this had happened the whole time being extremely defensive and rude to us. She said that she would only charge us for the smaller sized chicken baguette however we felt annoyed about how we had been treated.\n\nYou can see in the attached photo of the menu that the foot long baguette is not 3 different meats in one, you choose one meat and the obvious difference between that and the other baguettes is that it’s FOOTLONG however the chef was unable to admit this and would prefer and preferred to lie to us instead causing a scene and embarrassing herself. Will not be returning.\n\nShame as the food was decent but unfortunately they didn’t have the gumption to admit they’d run out of something and instead preferred to lie. Next time perhaps they should\nheed the saying ‘honesty is the best policy’ !\nRead more\nWritten November 1, 2019",
